cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Where, Not How Much: Fixed versus Adaptive Noise Schedules for Flow-Matching SDE Samplers at Low NFE"
abstract: >-
  A budget-conserving noise allocator for SA-Solver-style SDE samplers of flow-matching image
  models, with experiments on Anima, Flux 3 Klein and MOSS-Image at 6-15 network evaluations,
  a human perception study, and per-image metrics. Curvature-driven allocation showed no stable
  effect; error-driven allocation gave a small, model-dependent gain that a fixed per-step schedule
  reproduced.
authors:
